{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095579-which-legacies-are-spiritual-successors-of-various-ascension-groups","id":1095579,"title":"which legacies are spiritual successors of various ascension groups.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-22T11:41:31-07:00","id":1095579,"title":"which legacies are spiritual successors of various ascension groups.","content":"for instance i think there is one called perfected adepts that is based on the akashic brotherhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T16:12:17-07:00","id":1095644,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't this be in the awakening section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T07:51:40-07:00","id":1095910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095579-which-legacies-are-spiritual-successors-of-various-ascension-groups?p=1095644#post1095644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't this be in the awakening section?</div> </div> </div> </div>shit. that's what i get for posting while drunk<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T09:55:50-07:00","id":1095949,"title":"","content":"It could go either way, really. It involves both games, by its very nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T12:03:11-07:00","id":1095986,"title":"","content":"<br /> This is more a thing of early 1e Awakening, and fades away as the line develops.<br /> <br /> Subtle Ones (1e core) - Ahl-i-Batin<br /> Perfected Adepts (1e core) - Akashic Brotherhood<br /> Dreamspeakers (Legacies: The Ancient) - obvious<br /> Tamers of Stone (Legacies: The Ancient) - the Craftmasons<br /> Thread Cutters (Legacies: The Ancient) - the Euthanatos<br /> <br /> The Thrice-Great (Legacies: The Ancient) draw on Hermeticism, but in a different fashion from the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> The Celestial Masters of both games started out as explorers, but they went in very different directions. (Ascension's are in Mage: The Sorcerers' Crusade, one of the Order of Reason's founding groups, while Awakening's are in Keys to the Supernal Tarot.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T15:09:35-07:00","id":1096042,"title":"","content":"The Whipping Boys Legacy is tangentially related to the Cult of Ecstasy in my memory, in their pursuing of bodily sensations to reach transcendental awareness. <br /> <br /> The Choir of Hashmallim Legacy might pass for Celestial Chorus, since they're about summoning angels to kick ass of eldritch horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T00:13:12-07:00","id":1096192,"title":"","content":"The Uncrowned Kings draw on similar alchemical ideas to the Solificati, both pursuing self-perfection through refinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T01:31:58-07:00","id":1097456,"title":"","content":"thanks everyone. one last thing,given that i have little experience of awakening.. do these legacies affect the mages world view and affiliations in the same way that paradigm does in ascension? because of what i know magic in awakening seems to be mostly hermetic/kaballah/gnosticism/theosophy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T12:43:04-07:00","id":1097589,"title":"","content":"Legacies change what they use magic FOR - it doesn't change what magic IS, like paradigm does.<br /> <br /> In Ascension, paradigm isn't just how you create your effects (&quot;I aim my Particle Recalibrator and fire&quot;) but rather what you think magic is (&quot;my so-called 'magic' is simply the natural result of applying my revolutionary theories!&quot;). An Akashic's confusion upon meeting a Hermetic isn't just because the wand and ritual circle are unfamiliar tools - he is legitimately bemused about how he can possibly get fire to come out of that wand. <br /> <br /> Awakening has everyone sharing magic in a way - there's only five watchtowers, so 20% of all mages literally are powered by the same thing you are. Certainly the style changes with a Legacy, but it's not because magic changes for them - it's because they see a different reason for it. You might have a Fallen Pillar meet one of the Chrysalides. Both are Thrysus, powered by the Watchtower of the Singing Stone, and both use the Life arcana a lot. The purposes to which they put that nearly identical power are hugely, hugely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T17:38:46-07:00","id":1098295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095579-which-legacies-are-spiritual-successors-of-various-ascension-groups?p=1097456#post1097456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks everyone. one last thing,given that i have little experience of awakening.. do these legacies affect the mages world view and affiliations in the same way that paradigm does in ascension? because of what i know magic in awakening seems to be mostly hermetic/kaballah/gnosticism/theosophy</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Legacies change the mages' worldview and affiliations. But unlike capital-P Paradigms, they don't change how magic itself works - it's all symbolism in the end. However, Legacies give context as to how to interpret those abstract symbols into something more concrete. So more like a lowercase-p paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}